# Highlight Text (/docs/primitives/animate-ui/highlight-text)



## Installation [#installation]

```bash
npm install @animate-ui/react motion
```

## Usage [#usage]

The highlight is the element's background: give it one with your own classes.

```tsx
import { HighlightText } from '@animate-ui/react/primitives/texts/highlight';

export function Title() {
  return (
    <HighlightText
      text="Highlight Text"
      className="bg-linear-to-r from-blue-100 to-purple-100"
      inView
    />
  );
}
```

## Animation [#animation]

* The background grows from the left edge over 2s on an ease-in-out: slow at first, fastest midway, easing into place.
* With `inViewOnce={false}`, it resets off screen and sweeps again on the next entrance.
* `<AnimateUIProvider tempo>` paces the default duration.
* Under reduced motion, the text is highlighted at once.

## API Reference [#api-reference]

### HighlightText [#highlighttext]

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `text` (required) | `string` |  | The text to display. |
| `delay` | `number` | `0` | Delay before the highlight starts, in milliseconds. |
| `transition` | `Transition` | `{ duration: 2, ease: 'easeInOut' }` | Transition of the sweep. |
| `inView` | `boolean` | `false` | Wait for the text to be in view before highlighting. |
| `inViewMargin` | `string` | `'0px'` | Margin of the in-view area. |
| `inViewOnce` | `boolean` | `true` | Only highlight once. When `false`, it replays each time the text comes back into view. |
| `...props` | `Omit<HTMLMotionProps<'span'>, 'children'>` |  | Props of the root element. |

