# Splitting Text (/docs/primitives/animate-ui/splitting-text)



## Installation [#installation]

```bash
npm install @animate-ui/react motion
```

## Usage [#usage]

```tsx
import { SplittingText } from '@animate-ui/react/primitives/texts/splitting';

export function Title() {
  return <SplittingText text="Splitting Text" type="words" inView />;
}
```

Pass an array of lines with `type="lines"`:

```tsx
<SplittingText
  type="lines"
  text={['Introducing Splitting Text', 'Made with Motion.']}
/>
```

## Animation [#animation]

* Each piece fades in and slides 150px in from the right over 0.7s on an ease-out, 0.05s apart for characters, 0.2s for words, 0.3s for lines.
* `initial`, `animate` and `transition` customise every piece.
* Words never break in the middle; emoji and accented letters stay whole.
* `<AnimateUIProvider tempo>` paces the default transition and stagger.
* Under reduced motion (or with `disableAnimation`), every piece is in place at once.
* Screen readers read the text once, not piece by piece.

## API Reference [#api-reference]

### SplittingText [#splittingtext]

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `text` (required) | `string \| string[]` |  | The text to display, or an array of lines when `type` is `lines`. |
| `type` | `'chars' \| 'words' \| 'lines'` | `'chars'` | How to split the text. |
| `stagger` | `number` | `0.05 (chars), 0.2 (words), 0.3 (lines)` | Delay between two pieces, in seconds. |
| `delay` | `number` | `0` | Delay before the first piece, in milliseconds. |
| `initial` | `TargetAndTransition` | `{ x: 150, opacity: 0 }` | Hidden state of each piece. |
| `animate` | `TargetAndTransition` | `{ x: 0, opacity: 1 }` | Visible state of each piece. |
| `transition` | `Transition` | `{ duration: 0.7, ease: 'easeOut' }` | Transition of each piece. Its `delay` is added to the stagger. |
| `disableAnimation` | `boolean` | `false` | Render the text in its visible state, without animating. |
| `inView` | `boolean` | `false` | Wait for the text to be in view before animating. |
| `inViewMargin` | `string` | `'0px'` | Margin of the in-view area. |
| `inViewOnce` | `boolean` | `true` | Only animate the first time the text comes into view. |
| `...props` | `Omit<HTMLMotionProps<'div'>, 'children' \| 'initial' \| 'animate' \| 'transition'>` |  | Props of the root element. |

